# Upstream release checksum manifests, committed verbatim.
#
# These files are evidence, not source. A test recomputes each one's own sha256
# and cross-checks the digests compiled into `toolchain-manifest.ts` against the
# lines inside them, so a fabricated literal fails review rather than looking
# plausible. Their byte identity is the whole point.
#
# `-text` disables every end-of-line conversion git would otherwise apply.
# Without it a checkout configured with `core.autocrlf=true`, which is the
# default on Windows, rewrites LF to CRLF on the way to the working tree, the
# recomputed sha256 stops matching, and the failure looks like a tampered
# fixture rather than a checkout setting. `binary` would also imply `-diff`,
# and a reviewer needs to be able to read the diff when one of these changes,
# so `-text` alone is the right tool.
packages/daemon/test/fixtures/omp-releases/*.txt -text
